<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/15th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · War</p><h1 class="enc-title">Mad War</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1485">1485</a>–<a href="/years/1488">1488</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a> · Also known as Guerre folle</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Mad War was a conflict of 1485–1488 between the French crown, governed by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anne-of-france">Anne of France</a> during the minority of Charles VIII, and a coalition of nobles led by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/louis-i-duke-of-orleans">Louis of Orléans</a> and Duke <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/francis-ii">Francis II</a> of Brittany. The royal victory at Saint-Aubin-du-Cormier in 1488 ended the revolt and prepared the way for the union of Brittany with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/mad-war.jpg" alt="Mad War" width="320" height="125" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Patchy · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Castle_of_Vitre.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
